{#
  shinyFunc.R master template — shared plotting / helper functions

  This file is (almost) plain R: it is the shinyFunc.R sourced by the generated
  app's server, holding the functions every page calls. No per-dataset loop is
  needed except the trailing ATAC block.

  Map of what it defines, in order:
    - library() calls and aesthetic presets (font sizes sList, palettes cList)
    - safe_get_id(): config lookup with a helpful error
    - aesthetic helpers: g_legend(), ggsav(), sctheme()
    - per-page plotting functions used by the server partials:
        sc2Ddimr / sc2Dnum        -> dimred-zoom, dimred-sidebyside
        sc2Dcomp / sc2Dcnum       -> dimred-sidebyside comparison
        scDRcoex / *Leg / *Num    -> dimred-coexpression
        scVioBox                  -> violin-box
        scProp                    -> proportion
        scGeneList / scBubbHeat   -> bubble-heatmap
        sc2Dspat                  -> spatial-zoom, spatial-sidebyside
        scDRcellsplit             -> dimred-split
        scDRmarkerdt / *plot      -> deg-dimred
        scModuleScore             -> module-score
    - trailing {% for %} block: appends the trackplot helpers once per ATAC
      dataset (source of trackplot.R + scTrackplot), from partials/shinyFunc/.
#}
library(Matrix)
